cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this cookbook, please cite it as below."
authors:
  - family-names: Buchanan
    given-names: Glen
    website: https://github.com/glenbuchanan
  - name: "CESM2 LENS ML Readiness Cookbook contributors"
    website: "https://github.com/glenbuchanan/cesm2-lens-ml-readiness-cookbook/graphs/contributors"
title: "CESM2 LENS ML Readiness Cookbook"
abstract: "Seven chapters on NSF NCAR's CESM2 Large Ensemble (AWS Open Data): does the autumn ENSO state predict a wet Front Range winter? A supervised classifier built along NSF Unidata's Supervised Machine Learning Readiness spine, split by ensemble member, with refinement trials compared by a corrected paired test, one held-out test, and an out-of-period test on SSP3-7.0 winters under a protocol fixed before the run (self-attested), in which the edge does not replicate. Drafted with AI assistance (Anthropic's Claude) under the author's direction."
